{
	"_doc": "Homelands (scripts/space/homelands.gd, docs/CONTENT.md section 24). capital: every region place with `capital: true` (data/regions, the packs' regions) is the capital of its region's home_species. A capital is always an operational, friendly, single-race station of the size class `type` (data/station_modules.json types: one above the habitat), built with every signature room of its race (station_gen.gd), whose people are all its race: `people` (count, must = roles that are always aboard, roles = weights of the rest, guards = [least, most] friendly race guards). Its dock menu (campaign station_cfg, Homelands.menu) is the race trader and the race recruiter: `capitals.<race>.own` is the race's house line (id -> price: its tech pack parts and gear where it has them, else the dearest parts and gear its homeland sells), sold at `price` x the listed price, and it crowds the region's stock down to as many other items as it has own ones (at least half the shelf is the race's); `recruit` is the share of the recruit table the race holds. `line` is the arrival log line (name, race), `board` the capital's boarding offer (text, flavor; one %s = the name). wonders.<race>: a one-off landmark POI added to the sector of the capital node (sector.gd, poi type `wonder`, a beacon): `id`, `name`, `event` (the anomaly event it runs, data/packs/homelands_1; weight 0 and once, so nothing else rolls it), `art` (the drawer in scripts/view/wonder_art.gd), `radius` (px, the drawn size), `reward` {kind: blueprint or gear, id, tier (of the part, 0 for gear)}, `site` (optional on-foot site: kind, name, and for a station `race` and `module`, a module it must have).",
